3	// same object through is still read afterwards. This pass proves that on the Python tree, before the typed
4	// build runs, and sends every file it cannot prove to the dynamic build (src/dynpy), which shares as CPython
5	// does. Class instances are handles in the typed build, so only containers matter.
6	//
7	// The proof is an abstract interpretation over each function:
8	// - kinds: how deep a name's containers nest (0: never a container: a number, string, object or function;
9	//   UNK: unknown), so an int read out of a list is not tracked;
10	// - edges: pairs "object at depth a of place P may be the object at depth b of place Q", made wherever the
